00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090 align:start position:0%
 
it's been about two weeks since Apple's  new M2 iPad Pro has been in our hands  and honestly I'm kind of struggling to  figure out what's really new about it  seriously if you guys gave this thing to  me and told me I wasn't allowed to look  at the back of it where it now Sports  the new iPad Pro text I probably  wouldn't notice that it was the new M2  model unless I was specifically looking  for it and that's me a techie who's been  testing and reviewing iPad Pros since  before the 10.5 inch model got 120 hertz  Pro Motion in 2017. now imagine the  average person who isn't educated on all  of the differences between the previous  M1 and the new M2 they would probably  have no idea this is the new one and  that's also probably why the M2 iPad Pro  is already on sale on Amazon yes just  two weeks after launch right before the  holiday season when demand should be at  its best the new iPad Pro is already 50  off making it probably the first time  I've ever seen an iPad Pro get  discounted this quickly so to make sense  of that I'm gonna go through each of the  features that Apple showed off when they  marketed this M2 iPad Pro in their  promotional video but first I've got to  mention that it's not all bad news don't  worry there are some good things about  it that actually impressed me more than  I expected so stick around for that the  first major feature Apple showed off in  their video was the new M2 Chip with up  to 15 faster CPU performance and 35  faster GPU performance and after testing  multiple benchmarks like geekbench  speedometer 2.0 web browsing speed and  gaming tests I can safely say that the  math checks out and the M2 is actually  that much faster the only problem I have  is how Apple marketed the performance  making it seem like this is something  new with doctors now being able to work  with complex 3D models architecture CAD  Pro projects and photographers being  able to edit massive images faster than  ever the truth is that for many of the  apps people use even for photo editing  apps and others like they showed off the  M1 iPad Pro already handled those with  ease being perfectly smooth and having  no issues mainly because the apps on the  App Store are limited compared to high  performance apps you can find on Mac OS  so in the real world the M2 Chip isn't  really that big of a deal in terms of  real world performance and editing  experience the M1 was already doing a  killer job then Apple went on to show  that you can edit prores footage with  ease because of the built-in encoders  and decoders but as soon as we got our  new M2 iPad Pro in the office we  downloaded iMovie including the latest  update that just came out two days  before launch day and to our surprise  there was basically no difference  between the and one and the M2 which  means that their own app didn't support  the new encoders and decoders which is  one of the main things Apple showed off  in their video and yes I know that they  were using the new DaVinci Resolve app  but that's not launching for a while so  we use the app with the latest update  and it's a no-go now moving on Apple  also shut off the advanced cameras on  this new iPad Pro which can for the  first time record prores video making it  a complete movie studio right in your  hands but before I tell you the Shady  truth I discovered about this new  feature I've got to tell you about our  sponsor exters Black Friday bundle  that's 35 off and includes a convenient  key case for organizing Keys a cash clip  and the coolest wallet I've ever seen  the parliament wallet with this really  cool ejection mechanism for your cards  so check it out using the links below  now getting back to the new prores  recording mode when I began testing out  this new M2 iPad Pro I decided to see  how much better prores looked compared  to regular video formats but I was  stumped when I couldn't find the prores  format toggle in the camera settings I  thought maybe I needed a software update  nope it was on the latest software and I  still couldn't find it well it turns out  that Apple doesn't even allow you to  capture prores with the stock camera app  they literally force you to download  third-party software just to be able to  record prores so it turns out that the  whole prores thing is more marketing  than anything else especially if you  consider that the cameras on the new  iPad Pro have not changed one bit  compared to the previous model which had  cameras from the iPhone 12 generation  which are drastically worse than the new  iPhone 14 Pro Models so anyone in their  right mind would be shoot shooting  prores with that iPhone instead now the  next big thing that Apple showed off was  the fact that this iPad Pro now supports  Wi-Fi 6E which in itself is actually  really cool because it future proofs  this iPad but there are a couple of  important caveats the most important one  is that you need a Wi-Fi 6E router to  take advantage of the new six gigahertz  band which a lot of people don't have  including myself because they're still  very expensive but making it even worse  to take advantage of the six gigahertz  band Apple says you need a Wi-Fi 60  router that also has its 2.4 gig and 5  gig bands enabled and they strongly  encourage using a single network name  across all of the bands for the best  performance this this literally shows  that apple is not confident that the new  six gigahertz band will even give you a  better experience so they set it up in a  way that it automatically switches away  to the older bands if the connection is  spotty which kind of defeats the purpose  of Wi-Fi 6E if you're gonna be on the  old bands most of the time anyway but  nevertheless let's move on to the next  one we have the apple pencil hover  feature which is pretty neat and it'll  definitely help people see what they're  about to draw but it honestly seems like  a software feature they could have  implemented years ago if they really  wanted to but they held off until they  needed to add extra random features to  sweeten the deal but back to the rest of  the marketing video they literally just  rehashed a bunch of other software  features that are also available on  previous iPad models and that's it so  because of all of that I've got to call  this these smallest iPad Pro update of  all time even smaller than the a12z iPad  Pro in 2020 and that's why we've been  telling people to just buy the M1 iPad  Pro renewed on Amazon for as low as 605  bucks with a 90-day money-back guarantee  but wait there is some good news that I  mentioned in the beginning of this video  there is one area where I was pleasantly  surprised by the new iPad Pro and that  was in terms of gaming performance  because of the huge boost in graphics  performance compared to the previous  model the new M2 iPad Pro does quite  well for heavy Graphics related tasks  Dame Tech on YouTube tested out the new  iPad Pro with the most graphically  demanding game available on the iPad  genshin impact and it ran at 90 FPS  average a 16 Improvement compared to the  M1 which honestly isn't that much but  the impress aggressive part was the peak  temps being very low at just 36 degrees  Celsius meaning that the extra Graphics  overhead allows it to use less power  this basically means that this iPad Pro  will be set for the future when even  more demanding games and apps get  released and that's basically the one  reason you'd want to buy this new M2  iPad Pro future proofing you've got the  faster M2 Chip the Wi-Fi 6E support and  the Bluetooth 5.3 as well so it's  actually a great choice if you skipped  out on the last couple of iPad Pro  generations and you're finally ready to  upgrade especially since it's on sale  for 750 right now on Amazon and that's  just about the only positive thing I  have to say about the M2 iPad Pro so for  everybody else just wait until the next  one in 2024 because we're expecting a  new dual stacked OLED display a full  redesign with Max safe wireless charging  support the M3 chip built-on three  nanometer and probably more so with that  said if you enjoy this review click the  circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one check out one of  those two right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

